On Apr 4, 3:52 pm, strem...@rohan.sdsu.edu wrote:

>
> How about that when you die, quit, or ascend, it tells you the contents
> of named containers?  Then you can name a container "base" and see that
> you had foolishly left some essential kit behind...

That is an interesting idea indeed. Unfortunately, it doesn't seem
practical. The contents of containers not on the current level are not
easily accessible to the program at the time you would need them to
be.  The endgame routine would need to load each level you visited to
look for containers, or else keep a linked list of named containers in
memory at all times so it knows what levels they are on. If the
latter, then it needs to revisit that list every time you name
something, every time a gelatinous cube eats a chest, etc.



